/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:341:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:342:Assemble colored sprites into a central bar's notches, chaining successive pieces along fixed-width strips.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:343:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:344:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:345:- bg = most common color. Largest monochrome component is a solid "bar" with boundary notches (bg holes opening to its bbox edge).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:346:- Several smaller colored sprites scattered around the bar.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:347:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:348:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:349:- Each bar notch is filled by a root piece whose shape exactly covers the hole.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:350:- The root defines a strip (column-span or row-span) for its chain.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:351:- Successive pieces fill the bg cells inside the previous piece's bbox, locked to the same strip width.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:352:- Multiple chains grow independently from different bar notches.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:353:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:354:Key insight: The root piece's extent perpendicular to the chain direction locks the strip width for all subsequent pieces in that chain.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:355:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/2/prompt.md:356:</reference_puzzle>
